<div class="container">
  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

  <div class="about-image">
    <img src="/public/headshot.jpg" alt="Dominic Critchlow" />
  </div>

  <div class="about-content">

    <p>Dominic Critchlow is a forward-deployed product manager at <a href="https://www.ode.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ode with Anthropic</a> in New York, where he builds and deploys AI systems with enterprise teams.</p>

    <p>Previously, Dominic spent nearly a decade in national security. At the Department of Defense’s Chief Digital and Artificial Intelligence Office, he co-founded <a href="https://github.com/dod-advana/gamechanger" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gamechanger</a>, an AI-powered policy search platform. He built the first version himself; it grew to 1,500 users and a 25-person team, indexed millions of documents across the department, and was recognized by the National Security Commission on AI. Brookings later published a <a href="https://www.brookings.edu/articles/gamechanger-a-case-study-of-ai-innovation-at-the-department-of-defense/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">case study</a> on it.</p>

    <p>He later served as Chief Scientist for Booz Allen Hamilton in Europe, leading a 60-person engineering organization that built AI-enabled decision-support software for U.S. European Command and U.S. Africa Command.</p>

    <p>Dominic teaches graduate Big Data Analytics at Seton Hall University’s Stillman School of Business and serves as a Military Intelligence officer in the U.S. Army Reserve. He studied physics and computer science at Austin Peay State University.</p>

    <p>On his own time he builds small things: two iOS apps on the App Store, <a href="/pinned/">Pinned</a> and <a href="/helio/">Helio</a>; <a href="/flags/">Flags</a>, which tracks how often every country is mentioned in U.S. congressional records; and <a href="/airwave-ml/">radio and machine learning experiments</a>.</p>

    <p>The best way to reach Dominic is <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dominic-critchlow/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>. His code is on <a href="https://github.com/DomCritchlow" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.</p>
  </div>
</div>
